── Thinking ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Wait, I need to be careful with the string continuation here — `"\n\` followed by `             calibration...` — the `\` at end of line in a Rust string literal skips the newline AND leading whitespace of the next line. So `"risk meter: 1/5 pairs (88 snapshots, 2 validations)\n\` + `             calibration: cold start — 1/5 paired predictions, accumulating"` would yield `risk meter: ... \n` + `calibration: ...`. That's right — the `\` continuation strips leading whitespace on the next line.

